 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "I thought I had seen the sunset\nAt twilight in the vineyard's shade,\nWhen in the morning hours\nThe rose had had its flower,\nAnd by the sea, far away,\nShone like a gold-brown diamond.\nWhen did it pass from memory?\nCould time ever move away?\nWho could speak of sunset\nWithout saying sunset too?\nAh! there is none of you alone!\nNo woman can forget.",
